{
  "_note": [
    "The faces this hub offers, in the order a client should show them.",
    "This is content, not configuration: every household sees the same list until they change it. To change",
    "it, edit this file or drop a list of your own in data/characters.json, which wins entry by entry - a",
    "family that would rather see their favourite film characters than superheroes can do that without",
    "touching code, and the Hub UI writes exactly that file.",
    "`source` says which catalogue to resolve `page` against: superherodb for comic characters (a free",
    "key-less list of 563 of them, with clean portrait art and real metadata), wikipedia for everyone else.",
    "Pictures are fetched once and kept on this box, so a TV asks its own hub for faces and never learns a",
    "third-party hostname - and the picker still works when the internet is down."
  ],
